@Ordering_HostAddress = https://localhost:7105
@Identity_HostAddress = https://localhost:7102
@Catalog_HostAddress = https://localhost:7101
@Basket_HostAddress = https://localhost:7103
@Inventory_HostAddress = https://localhost:7104

################################################################
# PHASE 8 NEEDS FIVE SERVICES RUNNING:
#   Catalog, Identity, Basket, Inventory, Ordering
#
#   POST /api/orders
#        |-- GET  https://localhost:7103/api/basket        (the items)
#        |-- POST https://localhost:7104/.../reservations  (hold the stock)
#        `-- DELETE https://localhost:7103/api/basket      (best effort)
################################################################

### 0a. Alice
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@commerceflow.local", "password": "Str0ngPass" }

### 0b. Admin (needed to put stock in Inventory)
POST {{Identity_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@commerceflow.local", "password": "Admin#12345" }

@aliceToken = PASTE-ALICE-ACCESS-TOKEN-HERE
@adminToken = PASTE-ADMIN-ACCESS-TOKEN-HERE

### 0c. Find a real, active product
GET {{Catalog_HostAddress}}/api/products?isActive=true

@productId = PASTE-A-REAL-PRODUCT-ID-HERE

################################################################
# Setup
################################################################

### 1. Put 10 units in stock
POST {{Inventory_HostAddress}}/api/inventory/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantityChange": 10, "reason": "Phase 8 test stock" }

### 2. Alice adds 3 to her basket. Price comes from Catalog (Phase 5).
POST {{Basket_HostAddress}}/api/basket/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 3 }

### 3. Confirm the basket
GET {{Basket_HostAddress}}/api/basket
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

################################################################
# The happy path - note the body has NO items
################################################################

### 4. Place the order -> 201, status "InventoryReserved",
###    inventoryReservationId populated. Ordering read the items from
###    Basket using ALICE'S OWN forwarded token.
POST {{Ordering_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{
  "shippingAddress": {
    "line1": "1 High Street",
    "city": "Bengaluru",
    "postalCode": "560001",
    "country": "India"
  }
}

### 5. Stock moved: 7 available, 3 reserved, total still 10
GET {{Inventory_HostAddress}}/api/inventory/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 6. Basket is empty - cleared by step 4
GET {{Basket_HostAddress}}/api/basket
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

################################################################
# The refusals
################################################################

### 7. Order again with an empty basket -> 400
POST {{Ordering_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{ "shippingAddress": { "line1": "1 High Street", "city": "Bengaluru", "postalCode": "560001", "country": "India" } }

### 8. Ask for more than exists
POST {{Basket_HostAddress}}/api/basket/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 50 }

### 9. Place it -> 201 Created, but status "Rejected" with a reason
###    straight from Inventory.
###
###    201 FOR A FAILED ORDER? Yes. The POST created a resource - an order
###    record saying the attempt happened and why it did not work. The HTTP
###    status describes the REQUEST; the body describes the BUSINESS OUTCOME.
###    A client must read `status`, not just the status code.
POST {{Ordering_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{ "shippingAddress": { "line1": "1 High Street", "city": "Bengaluru", "postalCode": "560001", "country": "India" } }

### 10. Stock untouched, and the basket was NOT cleared - the customer
###     can lower the quantity and try again.
GET {{Inventory_HostAddress}}/api/inventory/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

################################################################
# THE POINT OF THE PHASE - do these two in order
################################################################

### 11. Fix the basket to something orderable
PUT {{Basket_HostAddress}}/api/basket/items/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{ "quantity": 2 }

### 12. NOW STOP THE INVENTORY SERVICE, then send this.
###     -> 503 + Retry-After: 5
POST {{Ordering_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{ "shippingAddress": { "line1": "1 High Street", "city": "Bengaluru", "postalCode": "560001", "country": "India" } }

### 13. Look at the order history. There is a GHOST ORDER, stuck in
###     "Pending" with no reservation, that nothing will ever move.
###
###     That is not a bug in the code - it is the honest cost of
###     orchestrating three databases with no transaction between them.
###     Phase 11 (saga) makes the flow resumable; Phase 12 (outbox)
###     guarantees the next step is never lost; Phase 13 (idempotency)
###     makes retrying the reservation safe.
GET {{Ordering_HostAddress}}/api/orders/my-orders
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### 14. NOW STOP THE BASKET SERVICE TOO and send this.
###     -> 503 again, but NO new order appears in step 13's list.
###     Basket fails at step 1, before anything is written, which is
###     exactly why the fragile call goes first.
POST {{Ordering_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

{ "shippingAddress": { "line1": "1 High Street", "city": "Bengaluru", "postalCode": "560001", "country": "India" } }

### 15. A ghost order can at least still be cancelled by hand - it is
###     Pending, which is a cancellable state. That is the only recovery
###     this phase offers, and it needs a human.
POST {{Ordering_HostAddress}}/api/orders/PASTE-THE-PENDING-ORDER-ID/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
